+    quat->covar kernel returns such rows for near-underflow scales (tiny
+    negative eigenvalues, |lambda| ~ 1e-9) on the garden 5K/14K snapshots; the
+    rasterizer never needs a Cholesky, so only this diagnostic coordinate is
+    affected. Repaired rows are counted in `stats`; every other row is
+    bitwise unchanged.
+    """
+    c = 0.5 * (cov + cov.transpose(-1, -2))
+    ref = c.diagonal(dim1=-2, dim2=-1).mean(-1).clamp_min(1e-30)
+    eye = torch.eye(3, device=c.device, dtype=c.dtype)
+    l, info = torch.linalg.cholesky_ex(c)
+    jitter = torch.zeros_like(ref)
